 "conclusion": [
  "Usage moved to NEAR Intents: it settled 82% of NEAR's DEX volume over the last 6 full months and $11.71B in the 90 days to 2026-11-04, 1.80× the 90 days before (T1, T2).",
  "Some of that value reaches NEAR holders, through buybacks rather than protocol fees. Since the fee switch of 2026-02-23, captured Intents revenue buys NEAR on the open market. In the 90 days to 2026-11-04 that was $4.8M, 27% of Intents' fees; NEAR's gas burn added $254.1K (C1).",
  "It is small next to the token. Annualized, captured value is $20.6M, 0.40% a year of NEAR's $5.17B market cap. Over the same months NEAR's total supply grew 2.5% a year net of burns, about $127.3M a year at $3.95; the buyback is 15% of that. The bought-back NEAR is held (2.18M NEAR in buybacks.multisignature.near), not burned.",
  "NEAR's weekly price does not move with Intents volume (r = 0.00 over 95 weeks, T4), and agent commerce is tiny next to Intents (T7). Small tickets are not an edge case: 48% of sampled swap legs and 47% of withdrawals were under $50 (P1). But in the quotes of 2026-11-05 14:34Z, 1Click refused all 6 agent-size tickets (under $50) on the agent's own routes (T9), so for now small agent tickets stay off Intents.",
  "Read as an investment case: the usage half is supported by the record so far (T1 and T2 describe the past; the forward tests F1 and F2 check it on new data), value capture exists but covers about 15% of issuance, and the agent half is still an option. The case for the token is that the captured share grows faster than supply; we would call it made when the buyback reaches half of net issuance over a 90-day window."
 ],
